  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi x)=1}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi x)=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\pi x & =\\pi (\\frac{1}{2}+2n) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}+2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\u2026,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={\u2026,-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{9}{2},\u2026}.\n$$",
